From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Support three mouse buttons, not sixteen

Each screen's ScreenInfo holds a binding for every button, context and
modifier combination, Mouse[MAX_BUTTONS + 1][NUM_CONTEXTS][MOD_SIZE]:
17 x 8 x 254 sixteen-byte entries, 540 KB, calloc'd.  With an MMU the
untouched pages cost nothing; without one all of it is RAM, a third of
twm's memory.  The WikiReader's touch screen is the first button and the
only one, but twm's default bindings name the first three, so the table
holds three, in 130 KB.  A press of a higher button is ignored and a
configuration that binds one is reported, as for any button past
MAX_BUTTONS.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Upstream: N/A sized for a one-button touch screen without an MMU
---
 src/twm.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/twm.h b/src/twm.h
--- a/src/twm.h
+++ b/src/twm.h
@@ -110,7 +110,7 @@
 
 #define NULLSTR ((char *) NULL)
 
-#define MAX_BUTTONS     16      /* max mouse buttons supported */
+#define MAX_BUTTONS     3       /* max mouse buttons supported */
 
 /* info strings defines */
 #define INFO_LINES 30
